337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 736 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, an LDR sensor is connected to pin 2 \(LDR_PIN\), and two LEDs are connected to pins 6 \(LED_PIN1\) and 7 \(LED_PIN2\). The second LED works opposite to the first LED.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 737 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the LDR as INPUT and both LEDs as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, both LEDs are turned OFF.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 738 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the LDR value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in ldrstate.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 739 0 R
/E (If light is detected \(HIGH\), the LED on pin 6 turns ON and the LED on pin 7 turns OFF. If there is no light \(LOW\), the LED on pin 6 turns OFF and the LED on pin 7 turns ON.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (So overall, the Arduino controls two LEDs in opposite ways based on light intensity.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
