484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 775 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, an LDR sensor is connected to pin 2 \(LDR_PIN\), three LEDs are connected to pins 3, 4, and 5 \(LED1_PIN, LED2_PIN, LED3_PIN\), and a buzzer is connected to pin 6 \(BUZZER_PIN\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 776 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the LDR as INPUT and all LEDs and the buzzer as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, all LEDs and the buzzer are turned OFF.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 777 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the LDR value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in ldrState.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 778 0 R
/E (If it is dark \(LOW signal\), all three LEDs and the buzzer turn ON. If it is bright \(HIGH signal\), all LEDs and the buzzer turn OFF.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (So overall, the system detects light intensity and activates multiple LEDs and a buzzer in darkness.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
