1050 0 obj
<<
/Title (In this class, students learn An LDR \(Light Dependent Resistor\) is a sensor whose resistance changes based on the amount of light falling on it. In bright light, its resistance decreases, and in darkness, its resistance increases. By connecting an LDR to a circuit with an LED, we can automatically control the LED based on light intensity. For example, the LED can turn ON in the dark and OFF in bright light, making it useful for applications like automatic street lights and light-sensitive switches.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 791 0 R
>>
